{"op":"add","path":"/elements/exec_summary","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"content":"Churn is most concentrated in the Enterprise plan, which averages 9650 in churn MRR and bleeds 6.97% of that segment's own gross MRR (Step 1). Across all months, churn tracks growth almost perfectly — Pearson r of 0.999 — meaning it is a structural loss rate applied to an expanding base, not an accelerating crisis (Step 2). The root mechanism is customer volume, not ARPU: volume explains 0.0527 of churn variance versus 0.6878 for ARPU alone, confirming the lever is onboarding and early retention at scale (Step 3).","variant":"insight"},"children":[]}}
