{"op":"add","path":"/elements/step2-insight","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"content":"Step 1 showed churn is largest in absolute terms in the highest-tier plan; Step 2 tests whether the overall churn trend is a business-health signal or just a growth artefact — and it is the latter: Pearson r = 0.999 with R² = 0.998 means growth accounts for nearly all monthly churn variance. Churn peaks in 2024-12 at 24200, and on average offsets 8.65% of each month's incoming growth. (Step 2)","variant":"insight"},"children":[]}}
